    <!-- Web (HTTPS) -->
    <string name="web_lead_title">What this adds</string>
    <string name="web_lead_body">DNS filtering already refuses whole tracker domains for every app. Interception goes further inside a browser: it removes ad slots and cosmetic clutter from the page itself, using EasyList rules that need to see the HTML.</string>
    <string name="https_caveat_title">Read this first</string>
    <string name="https_caveat_body">Since Android 7, apps ignore user-installed certificate authorities unless they explicitly opt in. In practice this decrypts Chrome, Edge and Samsung Internet — not Firefox, and not native apps. Everything else still gets DNS-level filtering.</string>
    <string name="https_caveat_warning">Android will show a permanent \"network may be monitored\" warning once the certificate is installed. That is expected.</string>
    <string name="https_ca_title">Root certificate</string>
    <string name="https_ca_ready">A certificate authority unique to this device has been generated. The private key never leaves the device.</string>
    <string name="https_ca_pending">Generated when the tunnel first starts. Connect once, then return here.</string>
    <string name="https_ca_trusted">Installed — this device trusts the certificate.</string>
    <string name="https_ca_untrusted">Generated but not trusted yet. Save it, then import it in Settings — interception cannot work until you do.</string>
    <string name="https_ca_steps">Android no longer lets an app install a certificate for you. Save it, then open Settings, search for \"CA certificate\", and choose Install a certificate → CA certificate → the file you saved. On Samsung it is under Biometrics and security → Other security settings → Install from device storage. Android will warn that the network may be monitored, which is expected.</string>
    <string name="https_install">Save certificate…</string>
    <string name="https_saved">Saved omnishield-ca.crt. Now import it in Settings to finish.</string>
    <string name="https_save_failed">Could not save the certificate. Try again.</string>
