    <string name="onboarding_skip">Not now</string>
    <string name="onboarding_1_title">Blocks ads and trackers</string>
    <string name="onboarding_1_body">OmniShield filters DNS for every app on the device, so trackers are refused before a connection is ever made. No root required.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_2_title">Why it asks for VPN permission</string>
    <string name="onboarding_2_body">Android only lets an app see network traffic through a VPN interface. OmniShield runs that tunnel locally on your device — nothing is sent to a remote server, and there is no account.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_3_title">Keep it running</string>
    <string name="onboarding_3_body">Android may suspend background services to save power. If filtering stops unexpectedly, exempt OmniShield from battery optimisation in Settings.</string>
